The highlight spacing is the spacing that is allocated for the selection symbol (if enabled) and is used to shift the list when an item is selected. This method allows you to configure when this spacing is allocated.

-   [`HighlightSpacing::Always`](enum.HighlightSpacing.html#variant.Always "variant ratatui::widgets::HighlightSpacing::Always") will always allocate the spacing, regardless of whether an item is selected or not. This means that the table will never change size, regardless of if an item is selected or not.
-   [`HighlightSpacing::WhenSelected`](enum.HighlightSpacing.html#variant.WhenSelected "variant ratatui::widgets::HighlightSpacing::WhenSelected") will only allocate the spacing if an item is selected. This means that the table will shift when an item is selected. This is the default setting for backwards compatibility, but it is recommended to use `HighlightSpacing::Always` for a better user experience.
-   [`HighlightSpacing::Never`](enum.HighlightSpacing.html#variant.Never "variant ratatui::widgets::HighlightSpacing::Never") will never allocate the spacing, regardless of whether an item is selected or not. This means that the highlight symbol will never be drawn.

This is a fluent setter method which must be chained or used as it consumes self

##### [§](#examples-5)Examples

```
use ratatui::widgets::{HighlightSpacing, List};

let items = ["Item 1"];
let list = List::new(items).highlight_spacing(HighlightSpacing::Always);
```

